W: Awake, my soul, and with the sun
W: thy daily stage of duty run;
W: shake off dull sloth, and early rise
W: to pay thy morning sacrifice.
W:
W: 2 Lord, I my vows to Thee renew.
W: Disperse my sins as morning dew;
W: guard my first springs of thought and will;
W: and with Thyself my spirit fill.
W:
W: 3 Direct, control, suggest, this day,
W: all I design or do or say,
W: that all my pow&apos;rs, with all their might,
W: in Thy sole glory may unite.
W:
W: 4 Praise God, from whom all blessings flow;
W: praise Him all creatures here below;
W: praise Him above, ye heav&apos;enly host;
W: praise Father, Son, and Holy Ghost.</miscellaneous-field>
